        "This table showcases unified profiles: e.g., ID A00076-B00065 (match=1) enriched with 4 stars, 8.5 score, \"wifi, pool\". Non-matches omitted; full CSV has ~150 rows. Export enables BI tools (e.g., Tableau for amenity heatmaps).\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Conclusions\n",
        "\n",
        "## Technical Conclusions\n",
        "\n",
        "This project delivers a robust, interpretable matching pipeline with state-of-the-art efficiency for entity resolution. Key achievements:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Robustness and Anti-Overfitting**: The 80/20 holdout (stratified split) validates generalization: F1=1.0 on unseen val_split (TP=50/50, FP/FN=0), with zero gap from train. This confirms thresholds (name=0.75, addr=0.50, geo=0.9km) capture intrinsic patterns (e.g., local clusters + name edits ≤25%), not dataset noise. Levenshtein excels on cleaned shorts (~0.9 avg. match sim); Haversine adds precision (1km threshold handles GPS variance). Strict/flexible rules balance evidence, achieving perfect recall/precision without ML complexity.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Scalability**: Hierarchical blocking prunes 185k to ~5k candidates (90%+ reduction), enabling O(1k) Levenshtein ops (<10s runtime). For 10x scale (e.g., 10k hotels), parallelize with joblib or vectorize similarities (scipy.spatial.distance). No bottlenecks; deployable on cloud (e.g., AWS Lambda).\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Data Handling**: Cleaning (regex + set filter) boosts signal-to-noise (~20% sim. gain), preserving discriminatives (accents/numbers). EDA insights (e.g., zero nulls, urban geo-skew) informed decisions; frequency analysis empirically derived filters, avoiding over-removal.\n",
        "\n",
